Subject: [PATCH] 1454: a "how I know them" sentence before the plan sentence
 goes (D739)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 53133, runs 2 and 3 of 3: the reply opened with a sentence on how the
person is reached ("... through Lika I know her, Lika knows her" / "found
in the network, ... knows her directly") before the plan sentence. It had
only one justification marker, so it stayed.

- Every form of "know" counts (ვიცნობ, იცნობს).
- New marker for the way through: მეშვეობით, გავლით, ქსელში, პირდაპირ
  (not as part of "direct contact"), through, via, and the ru/es forms.
- A paragraph before the plan is filtered sentence by sentence, so news
  sharing a paragraph with such a sentence stays and the sentence goes.

FOR_FRONTEND: 1849 tested, plus the tester's UX note on a blank member card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
